    ("ar", "The 'Product' in Social Marketing",
     "In social marketing, the 'Product' is often an intangible pro-social behavior, idea, or healthy practice rather than a tangible physical commodity.",
     "Social marketing campaigns sell desired behavioral practices (e.g. exclusive breastfeeding, boiling drinking water, wearing a helmet) to improve life quality.", 1,
     "Both (A) and (R) are true, and (R) correctly explains (A). The social marketing product is predominantly an intangible behavioral proposition (or an enabling device like ORS)."),
